design notes from production systems
pull-mode transfers (KVDirect7): engine initiates KV loads, manager doesn’t push. load_block is engine-initiated. ~2x peak memory reduction vs push mode.
CUDA IPC: cudaIpcGetMemHandle import latency is milliseconds. GPU\toshm\toGPU via async DMA ops instead.
page_size=128 vs vLLM’s 16: fewer, bigger transfers. 70b page at 128 tokens = 41.9MB vs 16-token = ~5.2MB. less ZMQ overhead, less granular prefix matching.
cache-aware routing (llm-d8): SubscribeToUpdates RPC = same primitive as llm-d’s KV Cache Indexer. extend proto with token hashes for prefix-aware routing (87% hit rates, 57x TTFT per llm-d benchmarks).
upcoming: vLLM RFC #31064, last-token hidden states alongside KV in P/D disaggregation. STORE_NOTIFY should support hidden states.
